&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Moloco:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Moloco is an AI-native performance advertising company, bringing the power of AI advertising to the open internet. Founded in 2013 by machine learning engineers who had built AI advertising systems inside the world&#39;s largest technology companies, Moloco began from a shared mission: to build that same engine for the open internet.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Today, Moloco is one company with two businesses, built on the same compound AI system. &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.moloco.com/moloco-ads&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Moloco Ads&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; is our AI-native performance advertising platform, helping mobile app marketers acquire, retain, and re-engage high-value users across the open internet. &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.moloco.com/moloco-commerce-media&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Moloco Commerce Media&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; is our AI-native retail media platform, enabling retailers and marketplaces to turn their platforms into thriving ad businesses. Both are powered by&lt;strong&gt; CARA (Compound Ad Recommendation Architecture)&lt;/strong&gt;, the AI system behind every Moloco product.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Moloco, we bring together those who&#39;ve already solved hard problems and those with the drive to. Here, we work on some of the complex problems in AI advertising, at a scale and level of sophistication very few companies can offer. &lt;strong&gt;Come build what&#39;s next.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Impact You’ll Be Contributing to Moloco:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Join Moloco as a Senior Growth Director and lead the strategic growth of some of our most important partners across EMEA. As a senior individual contributor, you will own a dedicated portfolio of top accounts, building executive partnerships

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About us&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our teams are putting the world&#39;s retailers online using cloud technology, robotics, AI and automation. Through the Ocado Smart Platform (OSP), we provide innovative technology and operational services to partners globally, supporting highly automated fulfilment centres and world-class online grocery operations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As our global footprint expands, we are continuously investing in robust health, safety, fire and environmental management to ensure a safe, compliant and high-performing working environment. This is an exciting opportunity to play a pivotal role in embedding a strong safety culture across our international operational services.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a &lt;strong&gt;Senior HSFE Specialist&lt;/strong&gt; to join our Operational Services team based in &lt;strong&gt;Hatfield (with travel)&lt;/strong&gt;, reporting directly to the &lt;strong&gt;Operational Resilience Director&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you will play a key part in establishing and driving Health, Safety, Fire, and Environmental (HSFE) compliance across our sites globally, embedding a proactive safety culture and ensuring consistent adherence to first-line requirements. Working closely with the HSFE Lead and operational leadership teams, you will provide day-to-day practical guidance and take ownership of delivering key first-line activities to support continuous improvement in safety standards across our operations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The role involves travel across our UK CFCs, with potential international travel to our global sites when operational needs arise.&lt;/p&gt;
